DECISIONS (stated assumptions)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. OUTPUT PATH NORMALIZED. The generator template names
   apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**, but that path is NOT a source root in
   apps/apple/project.yml (app-target sources: Sources, TeslaSync/{widget-
   primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,misc-surfaces,shared-surfaces},
   Localization) NOR in .swiftlint.yml `included`. A file there would neither
   compile into the app targets nor lint. The repo's real compiled feature root
   is Sources/Features/<Domain>/ — EVERY shipped admin page already lives in
   Sources/Features/Admin/ (ApiPlayground, AuditLog, DiskForecast, FleetAPI,
   FeatureFlags, TeslaOrders, …). Placed the page there for 1:1 consistency so
   it actually builds + lints. Still within the prompt's hard constraint
   (apps/apple/**). Precedent: the TeslaOrders sibling log recorded the same
   normalization.
2. FIRST-CLASS ROUTE (mirrors the directly-analogous TeslaOrders sibling). The
   shell route host (Sources/App/RouteHostRegistry.swift) is keyed by AppRoute,
   so a first-class, deep-linkable, testable destination (matching web's
   first-class /tesla-region page) requires an AppRoute case. Added .teslaRegion
   (segment "tesla-region", icon "globe" — the web Layout.tsx sidebar uses the
   globe icon + label "Region & API"). AppRouteParser resolves /tesla-region
   automatically by pathSegment (no parser edit needed). Group: web's
   "Integrations" sidebar group has no Apple peer; .account is the closest
   semantic bucket (the surface is features/settings/components/RegionSettings),
   matching where the TeslaOrders sibling placed /tesla-orders.
3. STRING KEYS = the manifest's literal parity keys region.title / region.subtitle
   (bare, not settings.*-prefixed). Rationale: (a) the manifest's PARITY items are
   literally "region.title" / "region.subtitle"; (b) the hosted RegionSettings
   feature surface (feature-view 0211) already resolves the SAME bare keys; using
   them keeps the page header and the embedded surface header in lockstep and
   makes the parity evidence match the manifest verbatim. Added to the master
   Localizable.xcstrings (default table) so TSPageTitle(LocalizedStringKey) and
   Text(LocalizedStringKey) resolve them.
4. DEFERRED LIVE SOURCE. The embedded RegionSettings surface binds through
   RegionSettingsModel ← RegionSettingsSource (P1/S8). The production live source
   (shared-core useTeslaUserRegion()/useRefreshTeslaRegion()) is wired centrally
   in the composition root, which is deferred app-wide (precedent:
   UnavailableVehicleCommanding in TeslaSyncApp; the TeslaOrders sibling seeds the
   same way). The registration therefore seeds an InMemoryRegionSettingsSource
   with a representative NA region so the page renders its populated `data` state
   out of the box — NOT production telemetry. The page is a pure function of its
   injected model; no networking added here. This is the page-level parity unit
   (2 strings); the RegionSettings data-binding is the separate unit 0211.

